  "notes": [
    "-AR verb with a spelling change: **z→c before e** to preserve the /s/ (Latin America) or /θ/ (Spain) sound, since \"ze\" is not a standard Spanish spelling. This affects the yo form of the pretérito indefinido (rechacé, not *rechazé) and every form of the subjuntivo presente and the usted/nosotros/ustedes imperative forms (rechace, rechacemos, rechacen).",
    "No stem change — this is purely an orthographic adjustment, not a stem-changing pattern.",
    "Past participle is regular: **rechazado**.",
    "*El comité rechazó la propuesta.* (\"The committee rejected the proposal.\")",
    "*Espero que no rechacen mi solicitud.* (\"I hope they don't reject my application.\")",
    "Related: *el rechazo* (rejection, noun), *aceptar* (antonym, \"to accept\"), other -zar verbs share this same spelling pattern (empezar, comenzar, alcanzar, cruzar)."
  ],
